Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:47:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] hbbs: the console's always-use-relay command changes
 only that setting

Upstream's "always-use-relay" ("aur") sets ALWAYS_USE_RELAY from its
argument and then also sends that argument on as the relay server list,
as "relay-servers" ("rs") does. Since patch 0010 names, in every message
it forwards between clients, the relay as written in that list, "aur Y"
made "Y" the relay every PC and controller was told to dial, until hbbs
restarted, and left the rotation list empty ("Y" does not resolve).

aur now changes the setting alone: "aur Y" turns it on, any other
argument off, and "aur" without one answers "ALWAYS_USE_RELAY: <on>",
as before.

tests/untrusted_input.rs: with -r 192.0.2.10, after "aur Y", "aur N"
and "aur y", "aur" answers the setting, "rs" still lists 192.0.2.10,
the relay response, punch hole report and relay request forwarded still
name it (before: "Y"), and a punch hole has the peer use the relay
(nat_type SYMMETRIC) exactly while the setting is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
